+## Device limits
+
+Direct readers of the original Metal device's limits receive the same measured
+values as the frontend getters. The field locations and widths are discovered
+through the original getters, following upstream a38e12a. On iPhone24A446,
+IconRendering reads the maximum 2D width and height directly from this table;
+an empty table rejects nonempty icon textures. The memory-pressure event source
+also retains process lifetime under ARC, following upstream46fdc91, so its
+existing resource-release handler remains available after initialization.
+Actual icon latency and Core Image program creation remain hardware checks.
+
 ## Memory reuse
 
-Unused owned image backing can serve later pooled or dedicated images. Image spares expire after ten seconds and are reclaimed on allocation failure or memory pressure; they have no byte limit. Unused buffer reservations share a separate 64 MiB device budget across memory types. The room worker rechecks demand and reuses a spare of the same pool and memory type before allocating. If foreground completions restore room during allocation, the new owned buffer stays spare with its address object intact. Plain unused backing of at least 256 KiB can be released by the existing room worker, with at most 128 MiB queued. Allocation failure reclaims queued backing before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks retain their release ordering.
+Unused owned image backing can serve later pooled or dedicated images. Image spares expire after ten seconds and are reclaimed on allocation failure or memory pressure; they have no byte limit. Unused buffer reservations share a separate 64 MiB device budget across memory types. The room worker rechecks demand and reuses a spare of the same pool and memory type before allocating. If foreground completions restore room during allocation, the new owned buffer stays spare with its address object intact. Owned blocks are freed on the runtime's existing free thread; a full 64-item queue releases on the caller. Allocation failure reclaims spares and waits for posted frees before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks retain their release ordering.
+
+The runtime keeps command counts in each open encoder and reuses unchanged resource-residency facts. Merge scratch can be lent to later encoders of the same command buffer, with its original barriers and leases. A shadow may remain current across command buffers only for tracked private memory owned by the runtime; heaps and external memory retain their required copies. `sheng-metal-flow=1` separately enables lowering, direct commit submission and pipeline warming for experiments; it defaults to off, and pipeline waits remain exact.
 
